      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-05T15:14:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>That looks like about as standard a superhero movie as you can get (a normal guy has something extraordinary happen to him and now he uses his enhanced powers to fight evil) plus some swearing. &nbsp;Does anyone really care if Deadpool is trying to do right by his girlfriend? &nbsp;<span>I'm surprised they didn't go more meta, going lighter on the origin story and heavier on the fourth wall breaking. &nbsp;</span><span>Seems to me like it's more evidence that Fox doesn't really know how to make good superhero movies and they just keep getting lucky with X-Men.</span></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:37.688Z",
